Z||000013||WGraffiKs||03-27-2000||03:26 AM||||Low CG- What's a slip angle?<BR>BTW, My preference was the Dunlop D40M2.  They really stick!! I used stock sizes, but they were a bit wider that the old Goodyear Eagles (NOT +4!!)  The D40M2 is hard to find now (no longer in production) and not as good as the D60A2 when it's wet out.  I have the D40's on the rear and the D60's on the front of my 86 GT.  The D60's slide more predictably.||||reg||1
